        },
        {
          "at_ms": 4700,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "id": "plab",
            "kind": "text",
            "text": "adjacent = cos θ",
            "x": 728,
            "y": 365,
            "size": 24,
            "color": "#1a1a1a"
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 5100,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "id": "qlab",
            "kind": "text",
            "text": "opposite = sin θ",
            "x": 728,
            "y": 300,
            "size": 24,
            "color": "#1a1a1a"
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 5600,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "id": "pyth",
            "kind": "latex",
            "tex": "\\cos^2 \\theta + \\sin^2 \\theta = (\\text{hypotenuse})^2 = 1",
            "x": 90,
            "y": 500,
            "size": 36,
            "color": "#1f7a3a"
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 6800,
          "do": "caption",
          "text": "On the unit circle, Pythagoras IS the identity"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "caption": "Compound angles: computing sin 75°",
      "narration": "Sin of a sum expands into products: sin A cos B plus cos A sin B. So sin 75 degrees is sin(45+30): plug in the familiar exact values and simplify to (root 6 plus root 2) over 4.",
      "duration_ms": 9000,
      "steps": [
        {
          "at_ms": 0,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "id": "sa",
            "kind": "latex",
            "tex": "\\sin(A + B) = \\sin A \\cos B + \\cos A \\sin B",
            "x": 90,
            "y": 80,
            "size": 40,
            "color": "#1a1a1a"
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 1200,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "id": "e75",
            "kind": "latex",
            "tex": "\\sin 75^{\\circ} = \\sin(45^{\\circ} + 30^{\\circ})",
            "x": 130,
            "y": 180,
            "size": 40,
            "color": "#1a1a1a"
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 2600,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "id": "e1",
            "kind": "latex",
            "tex": "= \\sin 45^{\\circ} \\cos 30^{\\circ} + \\cos 45^{\\circ} \\sin 30^{\\circ}",
            "x": 130,
            "y": 270,
            "size": 38,
            "color": "#1a1a1a"
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 4000,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "id": "e2",
            "kind": "latex",
            "tex": "= \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} + \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2}",
            "x": 130,
            "y": 360,
            "size": 36,
            "color": "#1a1a1a"
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 5400,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "id": "e3",
            "kind": "latex",
            "tex": "= \\frac{\\sqrt{6} + \\sqrt{2}}{4}",
            "x": 130,
            "y": 460,
            "size": 44,
            "color": "#1f7a3a"
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 6800,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "id": "chk",
            "kind": "latex",
            "tex": "\\approx 0.966",
            "x": 700,
            "y": 460,
            "size": 40,
            "color": "#1f7a3a"
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 7700,
          "do": "caption",
          "text": "Split the awkward angle into two familiar ones"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "caption": "The R-formula: one wobble, not two",
      "narration": "a cos x plus b sin x is really one wave: R cos(x minus alpha), where R is root(a squared plus b squared). For 3 cos x + 4 sin x that is 5 cos(x - 53 degrees) — and the max and min are suddenly obvious: 5 and minus 5.",
      "duration_ms": 8500,
      "steps": [
        {
          "at_ms": 0,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "id": "rf",
            "kind": "latex",
            "tex": "a \\cos x + b \\sin x = R \\cos(x - \\alpha)",
            "x": 90,
            "y": 80,
            "size": 42,
            "color": "#1a1a1a"
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 1100,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "id": "def",
            "kind": "latex",
            "tex": "R = \\sqrt{a^2 + b^2}, \\quad \\tan \\alpha = \\frac{b}{a}",
            "x": 120,
            "y": 170,
            "size": 40,
            "color": "#1a1a1a"
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 2300,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "id": "q3",
            "kind": "latex",
            "tex": "3 \\cos x + 4 \\sin x = ?",
            "x": 130,
            "y": 270,
            "size": 44,
            "color": "#1a1a1a"
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 3400,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "id": "R5",
            "kind": "latex",
            "tex": "R = \\sqrt{3^2 + 4^2} = 5, \\quad \\alpha = \\tan^{-1}\\frac{4}{3} \\approx 53.1^{\\circ}",
            "x": 120,
            "y": 350,
            "size": 36,
            "color": "#1a1a1a"
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 4800,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "id": "res",
            "kind": "latex",
            "tex": "3 \\cos x + 4 \\sin x = 5 \\cos(x - 53.1^{\\circ})",
            "x": 120,
            "y": 440,
            "size": 40,
            "color": "#1f7a3a"
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 6200,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "id": "max",
            "kind": "text",
            "text": "max value 5, min value −5 — one glance",
            "x": 120,
            "y": 510,
            "size": 26,
            "color": "#1a1a1a"
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 7300,
          "do": "caption",
          "text": "One cosine: max, min and period become obvious"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "caption": "Misconception: cos(A + B) does not split",
      "narration": "Cosine of a sum is not the sum of cosines. Check with numbers: cos 60 degrees is 0.5, but cos 30 plus cos 30 is about 1.73. Use the real formula: cos A cos B minus sin A sin B.",
      "duration_ms": 8500,
      "steps": [
        {
          "at_ms": 0,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "id": "wrong",
            "kind": "latex",
            "tex": "\\cos(A + B) \\neq \\cos A + \\cos B",
            "x": 110,
            "y": 120,
            "size": 46,
            "color": "#1a1a1a"
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 1300,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "id": "trap",
            "kind": "text",
            "text": "Same trap as (a+b)^n — the angle does not split.",
            "x": 120,
            "y": 220,
            "size": 28,
            "color": "#1a1a1a"
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 2700,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "id": "eg",
            "kind": "latex",
            "tex": "\\cos 60^{\\circ} = 0.5",
            "x": 120,
            "y": 320,
            "size": 44,
            "color": "#1a1a1a"
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 4000,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "id": "bad",
            "kind": "latex",
            "tex": "\\cos 30^{\\circ} + \\cos 30^{\\circ} = \\sqrt{3} \\approx 1.73",
            "x": 120,
            "y": 400,
            "size": 40,
            "color": "#b00020"
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 5300,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "id": "fix",
            "kind": "latex",
            "tex": "0.5 \\neq 1.73 \\;\\Rightarrow\\; \\cos(A+B) = \\cos A \\cos B - \\sin A \\sin B",
            "x": 110,
            "y": 480,
            "size": 34,
            "color": "#1f7a3a"
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 6200,
          "do": "emphasize",
          "target": "bad",
          "dur_ms": 900
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 7300,
          "do": "caption",
          "text": "Compound angles expand with the formula, never split"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
